# echo-server environment.
# On the VPS this lives at /etc/echo/echo-server.env (chmod 600), loaded by systemd.
# Locally, copy to server/.env (git-ignored) for `pnpm dev`.

# --- LLM provider keys (frontend never sees these) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Shared secret the frontend Settings page must supply as `Bearer <token>` ---
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 24
ECHO_API_TOKEN=

# --- HTTP port nginx reverse-proxies to ---
PORT=8787

# --- TTS provider (default: edge, free). Switch with TTS_PROVIDER. ---
# Gemini TTS uses GEMINI_API_KEY + the model below; returns neural audio.
# TTS_PROVIDER=gemini
# GEMINI_TTS_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview

# --- Optional: override task→provider routing without editing config.ts ---
# Defaults route both authoring (想说) and gloss (想懂) to Claude (anthropic).
# LLM_AUTHORING_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_AUTHORING_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_GLOSS_PROVIDER=deepseek
# LLM_GLOSS_MODEL=deepseek-chat
# LLM_AUTHORING_PROVIDER=gemini
# LLM_AUTHORING_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash   # or gemini-2.5-flash / gemini-1.5-pro

# --- Local dev only: call Gemini via the Gemini CLI (your Google login, no
#     metered key). Needs the `gemini` CLI installed + logged in. Leave the
#     model unset to use the CLI's default (API-style names like
#     gemini-2.0-flash may 404 in the CLI). ---
# LLM_AUTHORING_PROVIDER=gemini-cli
# GEMINI_CLI_PATH=gemini       # override if `gemini` isn't on PATH
# GEMINI_CLI_TIMEOUT_MS=360000

# --- Local dev only: call Claude via the Claude Code CLI (your subscription,
#     no metered API spend). Needs the `claude` CLI installed + logged in.
#     Production keeps the default `anthropic` (API key). ---
# LLM_AUTHORING_PROVIDER=claude-cli
# LLM_GLOSS_PROVIDER=claude-cli
# LLM_SCENARIO_PROVIDER=claude-cli
# LLM_SPLIT_PROVIDER=claude-cli     # 拆岛 (groups an island's sentences)
# LLM_KEYWORDS_PROVIDER=claude-cli  # 提取关键词 (extracts an island's key words)
# LLM_ASK_PROVIDER=claude-cli       # 随手助手 Q&A (/v1/ask)
# LLM_SCENARIO_MODEL=haiku     # scenario is output-heavy; haiku is much faster
# CLAUDE_CLI_PATH=claude.exe   # override if `claude` isn't on PATH
# CLAUDE_CLI_TIMEOUT_MS=360000 # raise if big scenarios still time out

# --- Behind a Cloudflare tunnel? (production = local backend via tunnel) ---
# The tunnel edge has a FIXED ~100s timeout (524). Our tasks don't stream useful
# bytes, so slow LLM runs get the connection dropped → the browser shows
# "Load failed". Route the slow tasks to fast models so they finish under 100s:
#   - scenario → Gemini Flash: reliable JSON + fast. (haiku flakes into prose;
#     sonnet ~160s → 524.) Uses GEMINI_API_KEY. NOTE the model name your key's
#     project actually has (gemini-2.5-flash here; 2.0-flash 404'd):
# LLM_SCENARIO_PROVIDER=gemini
# LLM_SCENARIO_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
#   - keywords / split → haiku (small JSON, ~25s, fits the cap):
# LLM_KEYWORDS_MODEL=haiku
# LLM_SPLIT_MODEL=haiku
#   - compose (想说) keeps the strong model (single sentence, fast, quality).
# See server/CLAUDE.md → "Cloudflare-tunnel timeout" for the full rationale.
